.TH HARDPOINT 6 "2026" "Hardpoint" "Games"
.SH NAME
hardpoint \- Operation Ironveil, a multiplayer arena first-person shooter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hardpoint
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hardpoint
is a multiplayer arena shooter in the style of a 2002 console FPS: twelve
original maps, five game modes, twenty-five weapons and bots that play the
objective. Every texture, mesh, sound and music track is generated at load
time, so the game has no asset directory and starts in well under a second.
.PP
Run with no arguments to open the game. Matches are played against a real
authoritative server, whether you host one yourself from the menu or join
somebody else's.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-connect " address"
Launch and join a server immediately. The address may include a port, which
defaults to 27015.
.TP
.BI \-\-server " [options]"
Run a dedicated server with no window. See
.BR hardpoint\-server (6)
for the options, which are the same.
.TP
.BI \-\-tracker " [port]"
Run a server registry that servers announce themselves to and browsers query,
for players who are not on the same broadcast domain. Defaults to port 27115.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH DEVELOPER TOOLS
These run headless and exit; they exist so the game can be checked without
playing it.
.TP
.B \-\-audit
Validate every map: geometry, navigation connectivity, spawns, objectives and
pickups. Exits non-zero if anything is wrong.
.TP
.BI \-\-stairs " [MAP|ALL]"
Walk the real player movement code along real paths across a map and report
anywhere a player holding forward would stop making progress.
.TP
.BI \-\-simtest " MAP [seconds] [players]"
Headless movement and collision soak.
.TP
.BI \-\-botmatch " MAP MODE [seconds] [bots] [skill]"
Play a full match headlessly, many times faster than real time, and report
scores, engagement rates and server tick cost. Set
.B HARDPOINT_CENSUS=1
to list every game event the match produced, which is how you tell a subsystem
that is not running from one that is.
.TP
.BI \-\-nav " MAP [height]"
Print a horizontal slice of a map's navigation graph as text.
.TP
.BI \-\-probe " MAP x z"
Explain one column of a map: brushes, standability and navigation nodes.
.TP
.BI \-\-icon " path [size]"
Write the application icon as a PNG.
.SH CONTROLS
Move with
.BR W ", " A ", " S ", " D ;
jump and respawn with
.BR Space ;
crouch with
.BR "Left Ctrl" ;
prone with
.BR Z ;
sprint with
.BR "Left Shift" .
Fire and aim are the mouse buttons, reload is
.BR R ,
melee is
.BR V ,
grenades are
.B G
and
.BR F ,
and
.B E
uses, plants and defuses. Weapons are
.BR 1 ", " 2 ", " 3
or the mouse wheel.
.B Tab
shows the scoreboard,
.B T
and
.B Y
chat,
.B Esc
pauses and
.B F3
shows the performance overlay. Everything is rebindable in Settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hardpoint/settings.cfg
Settings and key bindings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hardpoint/profile.cfg
Rank, experience, unlocks and career statistics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hardpoint\-server (6)
